From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: windows.security.authentication.web.core: the Web Account Manager, with no providers

Office's sign-in (OneAuth) asks the Web Account Manager --
Windows.Security.Authentication.Web.Core.WebAuthenticationCoreManager --
for the system's account providers (a Microsoft account, a work or school
account). The class did not exist: RoGetActivationFactory failed with
REGDB_E_CLASSNOTREG and the sign-in page ended with "Something went wrong"
(0x80040154).

The manager's statics (IWebAuthenticationCoreManagerStatics and ...4) are
implemented. No account provider is installed, so every provider lookup
completes with none -- Windows' answer for a provider it lacks; a lookup
of a provider's accounts, or a token request (whose provider could only
have come from here), is an invalid argument.

The asynchronous operation is windows.media.speech's, except that a
completed operation's result may be null.

Windows.Security.Credentials gains WebAccount and WebAccountProvider.

